/***************************************************************************
    parseCode notes (Clod, 2026-10-05, after SEQ 300)
    compileIn drives the code on a floor that carries the owner and pops it, so
    parseCode needs no processingCodE pair and no currentMETHOD or lastIndenT
    bracket -- the 2026-10-04 BLOCKER is gone with them.
    The owner is `action`, as in processCode: the CodE for a rule, else the argument.
    compileIn answers true or false; the BlocK rides back on pcReq.result.
    Read it as `blk = pcReq.result;` then `*blk`. `*pcReq.result` CRASHES (exit 139):
    the star binds to pcReq, which holds nothing.
    Never `if blk;` -- truth-testing the BlocK fires it (bear-trap 34).
***************************************************************************/

